{"created": "2022-04-01T07:39:58.183334+00:00", "modified": "2022-04-01T13:49:45.854189+00:00", "id": 6405084, "conceptrecid": "6379165", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.6405084", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.6379165", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6405084", "metadata": {"title": "Data-driven capacity estimation of commercial lithium-ion batteries from voltage relaxation", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.6405084", "publication_date": "2022-04-01", "description": "<p>Here are the datasets for the publication named &quot;Data-driven capacity estimation of commercial lithium-ion batteries from voltage relaxation&quot; published in Nature Communications. Experimental cycling data for three commercial 18650 type batteries (Dataset_1:NCA battery, Dataset_2:NCM battery, and Dataset_3:NCM+NCA_battery) are given, where each csv file corresponds to one cell cycling data. The cells are named as CY<em>X-Y_Z</em>-#<em>N</em> according to their cycling conditions. <em>X</em> means the temperature, <em>Y_Z</em> represents the charge_discharge current rate, #<em>N</em> is the cell tag. Each csv file has 9 columns, including cycle time (&#39;time/s&#39;), controlled voltage and current (&#39;control/V/mA&#39;), battery voltage (&#39;Ecell/V&#39;), applied current (&#39;&lt;I&gt;/mA&#39;), charge or discharge electricity (&#39;Q discharge/mA.h&#39; and &#39;Q discharge/mA.h&#39;), controlled voltage or current (&#39;control/V&#39;, &#39;control/mA&#39; and ), and cycle number (&#39;cycle number&#39;). In the impedance data, one representative cell from each cycling condition is chosen for the discussion in the main text. More detailed descriptions can be found in the zip file.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Jiangong Zhu", "affiliation": "Tongji Univerisity, Karlsruhe Institute of Technology", "orcid": "0000-0002-3780-4286"}, {"name": "Yixiu Wang", "affiliation": "University of British Columbia"}, {"name": "Yuan Huang", "affiliation": "Tongji Univerisity, Karlsruhe Institute of Technology"}, {"name": "R. Bhushan Gopaluni", "affiliation": "University of British Columbia"}, {"name": "Yankai Cao", "affiliation": "University of British Columbia"}, {"name": "Michael Heere", "affiliation": "Karlsruhe Institute of Technology, Technische Universit\u00e4t M\u00fcnchen"}, {"name": "Martin J. M\u00fchlbauer", "affiliation": "Karlsruhe Institute of Technology"}, {"name": "Liuda Mereacre", "affiliation": "Karlsruhe Institute of Technology"}, {"name": "Haifeng Dai", "affiliation": "Tongji University"}, {"name": "Xinhua Liu", "affiliation": "Beihang University"}, {"name": "Anatoliy Senyshyn", "affiliation": "Technische Universit\u00e4t M\u00fcnchen"}, {"name": "Xuezhe Wei", "affiliation": "Tongji University"}, {"name": "Michael Knapp", "affiliation": "Karlsruhe Institute of Technology"}, {"name": "Helmut Ehrenberg", "affiliation": "Karlsruhe Institute of Technology"}], "keywords": ["Lithium-ion battery", "Cycling datasets", "Degradation"], "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "6379165"}}]}}, "title": "Data-driven capacity estimation of commercial lithium-ion batteries from voltage relaxation", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6405084", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/6405084", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/6405084?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6405084", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6405084", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.6405084", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6405084/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6379165", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/6379165", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6379165", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.6379165", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:6405084/